          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a document refers to the J45 family, is that a code or a category?",
          "answer": "J45 is a **category**. The asthma coding document (coding-asthma-j45) refers to it as \"the category,\" and says it \"carries an explicit instruction to add a code identifying tobacco dependence.\" The document's title describes J45 as having \"severity and exacerbation axes,\" which suggests more specific codes sit under the category, but the retrieved text doesn't list them.\n\nThe lookup tool put J45 in a list labelled \"codes,\" but the source document itself calls it a category. In the coding documents retrieved, a category is a broader heading that can contain more specific codes, so a document that mentions J45 is usually pointing to the asthma group as a whole. The retrieved passages don't say which specific J45 code a particular record should use.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
